+// ======================= multi-row mat-vec (small batches, e.g. speculative-decoding verification)
+//
+// kernel_mul_mv_mr_<type>_f32_r<R>_nr0_<NR0>: dst[R rows] = src0 * src1[R rows].
+// Each simdgroup owns NR0 rows of src0. For every weight block it loads the quants once,
+// dequantizes them once into registers, and applies them to all R rows of src1, keeping R x NR0
+// accumulators per thread. The weight access pattern (lanes, block stride) is the same as the
+// corresponding single-row kernel_mul_mv_<type>_f32, so the weights stream from memory exactly
+// once per call instead of once per src1 row (mul_mv, grid.y = ne11) or once per 4-5 src1 rows
+// (mul_mv_ext). src1 rows beyond ne11 (last threadgroup row) are clamped to the last valid row
+// and not written.
+//
